{"id": "EUVD-2026-103638", "enisaUuid": "b4bfd751-337c-3767-bf15-1a9ec0a1c0a3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/debug: Fix NULL pointer dereference in debug_info_copy()\n\nWhen debug_register_static() fails, it clears areas, active_pages and\nactive_entries but leaves the area bounds unchanged. Copying such an\narea, either by opening its view file or via debug_dump(), makes\ndebug_info_copy() dereference the NULL pointers.\n\nSkip the copy loop when the source has no areas.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13decd3b3b3a4d8a2e603fb8c9ffde0c6be3c225", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a19bede30f0da5ae56782edac62b5998a7434cba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33f706884821da9cb55b650b7b1d4f2bdf800137", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2de9c458cc49d8db6408a7c5fbf0c7c94fe4d52b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c6af88fbefbe77608b77409df23a1617e28398c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c593f38e1cdb92f87d01be4c4e5ac12417b1454b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/012bfcd5a51082d5a65f096dfb9ca652b5267965"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98593", "GHSA-v4qr-c46c-6qg3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "040ad67d-64cb-3ef6-8465-2dc29d74f934", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "16414bfb-0312-370f-97d2-8edd6846f71c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d72541f945127b4873dace501406a1bc8cd8e1e9 <33f706884821da9cb55b650b7b1d4f2bdf800137"}, {"id": "18016326-a17f-36c2-9eb0-8296aeab3899", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "1b75e654-e588-3d3b-99dd-10c825808078", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d72541f945127b4873dace501406a1bc8cd8e1e9 <9c6af88fbefbe77608b77409df23a1617e2839